- *The pyramid habit:* for every award family, learn the TOP first (highest honour), then one rung below. Traps feed on pyramid swaps.
- *The currency rule:* award names and winners change. Whatever your sources said last year, re-verify the current holders close to exam day.

= Static GK Map 2 — Important Days and Famous Firsts

Days and firsts are pure recall — so the memory method matters more than the material. Learn days *in month order* in small clusters of five, never as a shuffled list. Learn firsts as *chains*: first President → first woman President → first President born in the 21st-century era of officeholders you verify near exam time.

