= Practice Questions (Exam Pattern)

Ten questions in the CUET UG style — a mix of static recall, pairing, and NOT-statements, exactly the shapes this chapter rehearsed. Each correct answer earns $+5$; each incorrect one costs $-1$, so apply graded confidence.

#mcq(1, [The book "Gitanjali", which brought the Nobel Prize in Literature to India in 1913, was written by:], (
  [Munshi Premchand], [Rabindranath Tagore], [Jawaharlal Nehru], [R.K. Narayan],
))

#mcq(2, ["Wings of Fire" is the autobiography of:], (
  [Mahatma Gandhi], [Jawaharlal Nehru], [A.P.J. Abdul Kalam], [Khushwant Singh],
))

#mcq(3, [Which of the following pairs is INCORRECTLY matched?], (
  [Jnanpith Award — Literature], [Dadasaheb Phalke Award — Cinema], [Param Vir Chakra — Wartime military valour], [Bharat Ratna — Sports],
))

#mcq(4, [India's National Sports Day, marking the birth anniversary of hockey legend Major Dhyan Chand, falls on:], (
  [29 August], [5 September], [22 April], [28 February],
))

#mcq(5, [National Science Day marks the discovery of the Raman Effect on 28 February. In which year did C.V. Raman make this discovery?], (
  [1913], [1928], [1947], [1950],
))

#mcq(6, [Which of the following is the highest PEAK located in India?], (
  [Mount Everest], [K2], [Kanchenjunga], [Nanda Devi],
))

#mcq(7, [In India's constitutional structure, the head of the GOVERNMENT (as distinct from the head of the State) is:], (
  [the President], [the Prime Minister], [the Chief Justice], [the Vice President],
))

#mcq(8, [Who was the first woman President of India?], (
  [Indira Gandhi], [Pratibha Patil], [Sarojini Naidu], [Droupadi Murmu],
))

#mcq(9, [Chandrayaan-3 made India the first country to soft-land near which region of the Moon?], (
  [the north pole], [the south polar region], [the far side centre], [the Sea of Tranquility],
))

#mcq(10, [Which of the following statements about India's Republic Day is TRUE?], (
  [It marks the Constitution coming into force on 26 January 1950], [It marks independence from colonial rule in 1947], [It is celebrated on 15 August every year], [It commemorates the first general elections],
))

= Detailed Solutions

Each solution shows the working, not just the verdict — cover the answer line, attempt the reasoning, then compare.

#solution(1, [Static pair from the books table: Gitanjali — Tagore — 1913 Nobel in Literature, Asia's first. Premchand belongs to Godan; Nehru to The Discovery of India.], answer: [B])

#solution(2, [Wings of Fire is Kalam's autobiography — the Missile Man who became President. Gandhi's is My Experiments with Truth; Nehru's is Discovery of India.], answer: [C])

#solution(3, [The pyramid check: Bharat Ratna honours ANY field as India's highest CIVILIAN award — it is not a sports award. The other three pairs sit correctly in their fields.], answer: [D])

#solution(4, [29 August — Major Dhyan Chand's birth anniversary. The distractors are all real days from your table: Teachers' (5 Sept), Earth (22 Apr), Science (28 Feb).], answer: [A])

#solution(5, [National Science Day (28 February) marks the Raman Effect discovered in 1928 — the work that later brought India's first science Nobel (1930). 1947 and 1950 belong to independence and the Constitution.], answer: [B])

#solution(6, [The world-vs-India trap: Everest is the world's highest but lies in Nepal. Kanchenjunga — on India's border with Nepal — is the highest peak located in India.], answer: [C])

#solution(7, [The two-heads rule: President = head of the STATE; Prime Minister = head of the GOVERNMENT, running it day to day. The judiciary interprets; it does not head the government.], answer: [B])

#solution(8, [Pratibha Patil held the office from 2007 to 2012 — the first woman President. Indira Gandhi was Prime Minister, not President; Naidu was the first woman Governor of a state and later President of the Congress; the current officeholder should always be re-verified near exam day.], answer: [B])

#solution(9, [The grid chain: Chandrayaan-3 (23 August 2023, ISRO) soft-landed near the lunar SOUTH POLAR region — a first for any country. The north pole and other sites belong to earlier missions of other nations.], answer: [B])

#solution(10, [Republic Day = 26 January 1950, the day the Constitution came into force. Option B describes Independence Day (15 August) — the classic day-date swap.], answer: [A])

