= Your GK Habit Card

Everything this chapter taught, shrunk to one card you can pin above your desk. The card works because it asks nothing heroic: fifteen minutes on ordinary days, one consolidation sitting a month, one verification hour before the exam. Run it exactly as written for eight weeks and GK stops being a subject you fear and becomes a section you finish early.

#table(
  columns: (1.15fr, 1.55fr, 2.1fr),
  table.header[*Rhythm*][*The ritual*][*What it produces*],
  [Daily · 15 min], [Headlines + one deep story + one note grid], [Six category pages of current facts, growing quietly],
  [Weekly · 15 min], [Scan all static tables made so far], [Tables stay warm — no re-learning ever needed],
  [Monthly · 45 min], [Consolidate grids into one revision page per category], [A shrinking stack of pages instead of a pile of loose notes],
  [Pre-exam · 1 hour], [The currency check from one reliable source], [No stale officeholders, no renamed-award slips],
)

- *The rule that makes the card work:* never read a significant event without filling its grid — reading without noting is entertainment, not preparation.
- *The rule that protects your score:* graded confidence — full recall answers, partial recall eliminates, blank facts walk away.

